{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/812904-julii-for-second-edition","id":812904,"title":"Julii for Second Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-20T14:35:05-08:00","id":812904,"title":"Julii for Second Edition","content":"So this is a request I see pop up from time to time - How to convert the Julii to Second Edition rules. Obviously this is a pretty easy task from a mechanical standpoint, since the Bane is the only thing that needs updating, and even the original bane kind of works. A number of suggestions have been made, and they all make great options, depending on what themes of the Julii you wish to emphasize. But I was not satisfied with just a quick and dirty patch to the Clan Bane. I wanted to give the whole Clan writeup a Second Edition style facelift, and bring the Clan of the Founders into tonight's Requiem. So I've written up a document for them in the style of the Clan entries in the Who We Are Tonight chapter of Vampire: the Requiem Second Edition. I hope that I have done a faithful job in capturing the tone and style of the writer responsible for those fantastic pieces.<br /> <br /> So, without further introduction, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B0KDN_qcgXvwQkpjaTRxOEpFQXM/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here is my take</a> on the Julii for Second Edition. Special thanks to Yossarian for helping me make it <i>look</i> like something out of Second Edition, in addition to sounding like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-20-2016, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpat